  "notes": "Boot a Black Rose ROM from an empty NVRAM with the coin door open (public 22 released) and PinMAME's built-in mechanisms disabled; the scenario names no game. Leave the fresh-NVRAM loop with Escape and open the service menu. Start T.1 SWITCH EDGES, then drive each fitted playfield and cabinet switch the manual prints (all but the coin door 22, the always-closed 24, the slam tilt 21 and the start button 13) and the Fliptronic buttons 112, 114 and 116 to public 1 and back to 0, holding each level for 1.5 s. The ROM's top display line names a switch while it reads it as active, so the edge that brings a name up shows which public level the ROM treats as active and pairs the ROM's own name with each public address.",
